723	    // audio or revoke its current blob URL here. Destroy fires on LV
724	    // reconnect/re-mount (long phone sleep → server LV process times out
725	    // → client re-mount on wake) — and the <audio> element survives
726	    // (phx-update="ignore"). Pausing or revoking would interrupt the
727	    // user's listening session at exactly the moment they wake the phone
728	    // hoping playback continues. If the player is genuinely going away
729	    // (user navigates off the reader), the <audio> element gets removed
730	    // from the DOM, which auto-pauses it — no explicit pause needed.
